WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.106
Euclid's Elements, Book One, Proposition Forty-Five.

2
00:00:04.106 --> 00:00:09.635
Construct, in a given angle, a parallelogram equal in area to a given polygon.

3
00:00:09.635 --> 00:00:14.385
Let A B C D be the given polygon and E the given rectilineal angle.

4
00:00:14.385 --> 00:00:20.410
We construct a parallelogram equal in area to polygon A B C D in an angle equal to E.

5
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:26.309
Construct segment D B, dividing polygon A B C D into triangles A B D and D B C.

6
00:00:26.309 --> 00:00:34.770
By Proposition Forty-Two, construct parallelogram F K H G equal in area to triangle A B D in angle H K F equal to angle E.

7
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:44.480
Then, by Proposition Forty-Four, apply to segment G H parallelogram G H M L equal in area to triangle D B C in angle G H M equal to angle E.

8
00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:51.081
Since angle E equals both angle H K F and angle G H M, angle H K F equals angle G H M.

9
00:00:51.081 --> 00:00:56.974
Add angle K H G to each; then angles F K H and K H G equal angles K H G and G H M.

10
00:00:56.974 --> 00:01:14.797
By Proposition Twenty-Nine, interior angles F K H and K H G between parallels F K and G H sum to two right angles, so angles K H G and G H M also sum to two right angles; thus by Proposition Fourteen, K H and H M form a single straight segment K M.

11
00:01:14.797 --> 00:01:21.984
Again, since transversal H G cuts parallels K M and F G, alternate angles M H G and H G F are equal.

12
00:01:21.984 --> 00:01:35.710
Add angle H G L to each; since interior angles M H G and H G L sum to two right angles, angles H G F and H G L also sum to two right angles, so F G and G L form a single straight segment F L.

13
00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:50.874
Because F K and M L are each equal and parallel to H G, they are equal and parallel to one another, and segments K M and F L joining their extremities are also equal and parallel, making K F L M a parallelogram.

14
00:01:50.874 --> 00:02:07.260
Finally, since triangle A B D equals parallelogram F K H G and triangle D B C equals parallelogram G H M L, the whole polygon A B C D equals the whole parallelogram K F L M in angle F K M equal to angle E, as was required to do.
